<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">20052026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Israel planned to install former president Mahmoud Ahmadinejad as Iran's post-war leader, according to a New York Times account of the summer war.</s> <s>The operation included a jailbreak strike on the Revolutionary Guard post guarding his house arrest in Tehran's Narmak district — it injured him instead.</s> <s>Ahmadinejad vanished afterwards, and the alternative-government scenario collapsed, reframing the war not as a defensive strike but as a failed political project.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Vladimir Putin arrived in Beijing five days after Donald Trump left.</s> <s>China hosted both leaders inside the same compound within a single week — positioning itself as indispensable to Washington and Moscow alike, and quietly refusing the G-two framing Trump had hoped to walk away with.</s> <s>Forty bilateral agreements await signature, though Moscow and Beijing haven't yet committed on the oil routing question now that Hormuz traffic remains disrupted.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A Pakistani court sentenced twenty-three-year-old Umar Hayat to death for murdering seventeen-year-old TikTok star Sana Yousaf, who'd rejected him online.</s> <s>He broke into her home, shot her, and admitted the killing within a month.</s> <s>Pakistan's Human Rights Commission logged roughly four hundred femicides last year — most never reach a verdict, which makes Sana's name unusually one history will remember.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s><sub alias="Jneem">JNIM</sub>, al-Qaeda's Sahel affiliate, killed Mali's defence minister and blockaded Bamako on April twenty-fifth.</s> <s>The group's been targeting fuel and power since September of last year, and the new siege cuts the Dakar trade corridor that the capital depends on.</s> <s>The junta that expelled France in twenty-twenty-two now cannot hold the country it took.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Nigerian and American airstrikes killed Abu Bilal al-Minuki, named as Islamic State's global operations director, alongside one hundred seventy-five claimed fighters in the country's northeast.</s> <s>It's the first announced kinetic operation under Trump's reactivated Africa Command posture.</s> <s>No independent body has verified the count — the question of who exactly the other one hundred seventy-four were remains unanswered.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Papua New Guinea's Highlands now runs a working market for hired gunmen — locals call them hiremen, priced and contracted like any other labour.</s> <s>Members of parliament use district development funds to pay militias; the militias deliver votes; the cycle closes.</s> <s>No announced policy targets the patronage chain that makes the violence rational, so the gunmen remain symptoms, not causes.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Chilean President Kast is fast-tracking lithium concessions on the Atacama salt flats, merging mining and economy under a single minister.</s> <s>Chile holds roughly thirty-six percent of global lithium reserves, and Kast intends to court both Washington and Beijing as customers without choosing between them.</s> <s>Each cubic metre of brine pumped is freshwater removed from Lickanantay communities — the geopolitics of clean energy is being paid for by Andean water tables.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A former Sudanese energy minister argues that the country's electricity map predicted its war.</s> <s>The grid served Khartoum and Port Sudan; Darfur and Kordofan received almost nothing — a structural deficit, he writes, that wasn't a casualty of conflict but a precondition for it.</s> <s>His paper calls for forty percent hydro and thirty percent solar by twenty-forty, which presumes a state still capable of building.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Brussels pledged exceptional support for European farmers as urea fertiliser prices surged on Gulf shipping disruption.</s> <s>Nearly half of the world's traded urea moves through the Strait of Hormuz, and Gulf plants have cut or halted production as gas supply faltered.</s> <s>A war in the Gulf is now showing up as a fertiliser bill in Polish and French wheat fields, and the union's absorbing the cost rather than confronting the cause.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Volkswagen, Foton, and JAC Motors will all open vehicle-assembly plants in Uzbekistan by year's end.</s> <s>President Mirziyoyev signed an export package that puts German and Chinese rivals onto the same factory floors in Tashkent, and later the Angren free economic zone.</s> <s>Central Asia's quietly become the rare place where the world's two largest auto blocs compete without anyone being asked to choose between them.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The United Kingdom's Climate Change Committee says adaptation costs less than the damage of doing nothing.</s> <s>It's called for eleven billion pounds in extra annual investment — mostly private — on flood defences, cooling, and water supply, feeding into the country's fourth climate risk assessment due in twenty-twenty-seven.</s> <s>Only six of forty-six adaptation priorities are currently on track, which means most of the investment hasn't yet happened.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>An artificial-intelligence system called Robin scanned five hundred fifty-one scientific papers in thirty minutes, surfacing drug candidates for leukaemia and macular degeneration that human researchers had missed.</s> <s>Two papers in Nature validate the approach, alongside Google's Co-Scientist tool.</s> <s>The real shift isn't drug discovery being automated — it's the scientific literature itself becoming searchable for cross-field connections no single specialist could see.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A multi-university survey of American researchers documents what a year of grant freezes and visa restrictions has done to United States science.</s> <s>Project cancellations, lab layoffs, and a quiet exodus to Europe and East Asia run across institutions — the federal pipeline that anchored the research base since the Second World War is being voluntarily dismantled.</s> <s>For the listener, this is a story about state capacity, not partisan politics.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Filipino virtual assistants are ghostwriting LinkedIn for Western executives at seven dollars an hour.</s> <s>A single worker may operate up to forty accounts simultaneously — artificial intelligence generates the posts, a human launders them through a real account, the executive collects the reputational dividend.</s> <s>This is what the AI labour economy actually looks like, in sha'Allah we'll see it named honestly... not robots replacing workers, but underpaid workers in the Global South laundering machine output for richer ones.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Investigators have confirmed that a Huawei zero-day vulnerability caused Luxembourg's nationwide telecom outage last year.</s> <s>Single-vendor concentration meant one flaw took all telephony offline, and Huawei still hasn't acknowledged the flaw publicly.</s> <s>A year on, no European Union audit has reviewed how many other member states depend on the same equipment — and the unexamined dependency remains.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>